# Runner sentinel files (emit_outcome IPC between experiment script and runner).
# Transient + machine-local; treated as telemetry by governance/explorer (skip lists),
# never read as evidence. Committing them dirtied the hub shared checkout and wedged
# the phase3 writers (no autostash). Untracked 2026-06-02.
evidence/experiments/_runner_signals/

# IGW self-audit report -- machine-local diagnostic, regenerated daily by com.ree.igwaudit
evidence/planning/igw_routine_audit.md

# Public-explorer local review artifact (never publish)
public_explorer_redaction_report.md

# Mobile access concrete local runbook and optional rendered helper.
docs/mobile_access.local.md
mobile_help.local.html

# SHP-1 shadow status-head projector output (status_history_plane:SHP-1).
# Regenerable, read-only projection (scripts/project_status_head.py); never canonical.
scratch/

# igw_routine_tick.py pause sentinel -- local flag, never committed (matches
# IGW's own critical-loop writer, which only ever .write_text()s it).
evidence/planning/.igw_routine_pause

# Oversized companion artifact quarantined 2026-08-12 (184.6MB, GitHub 100MB blob limit). Real copy kept locally on hub + Mac; see the .placemarker.json sibling.
evidence/experiments/v3_exq_921_mech490_sleep_commitgate_spawn_matched/v3_exq_921_mech490_sleep_commitgate_spawn_matched_20260812T152532Z_episode_log.json

# V3-EXQ-978 fishtank companion -- real bytes stay on Mac + hub via SSH; git holds only the .placemarker.json sibling (same convention as 921).
evidence/experiments/v3_exq_978_sd018_directional_field_fishtank/runs/v3_exq_978_sd018_directional_field_fishtank_20260903T111718Z_v3/v3_exq_978_sd018_directional_field_fishtank_20260903T111718Z_episode_log.json

# Same V3-EXQ-978 bytes, at the FLAT path a worker recovery left behind on
# ree-cloud-3 (sha256-identical to the nested copy above; verified 2026-09-23,
# chip-20260923-placemarker-copy-audit). Ignored for the same reason as the
# nested path -- this content is deliberately off git -- but the flat spelling
# needs its own line, and without it two things went wrong on that box:
#   1. the runner's prepull stash selects on `?? ` with --ignored=no, so it
#      stashed and popped this file before EVERY pull -- ~1440 cycles a day,
#      1020+ by 2026-09-15 -- and each cycle is a chance for the pop to fail,
#      which is the documented silent-loss path (CLAUDE.md, stash audit).
#   2. the stuck-path escalation then advised that "this file is the only copy
#      and needs manual delivery", which is FALSE here: it is the third copy of
#      content whose canonical home is the placemarker'd nested path, with two
#      verified durable copies (Mac + hub). A true warning with a wrong remedy.
# Ignoring it ends the churn, silences the false escalation, and blocks it from
# being swept into a commit that would land bytes git deliberately excludes.
evidence/experiments/v3_exq_978_sd018_directional_field_fishtank_20260903T111718Z_episode_log.json

# Derived evidence read-model (derived_evidence_index:P1). A disposable SQLite
# projection of the git-tracked manifests + claim_evidence.v1.json, rebuilt from
# scratch by evidence/experiments/scripts/build_experiment_indexes.py on every
# governance run. NEVER a source of truth -- deleting it is always safe, and
# committing it would create a second, mutable "record" beside the signed one.
# See evidence/experiments/scripts/derived_evidence_db.py.
evidence/experiments/.derived/

# Lock sentinel for the serialised review_tracker.json read-modify-write
# (serve.py _review_tracker_guard). Machine-local, zero-length, never content.
evidence/experiments/review_tracker.json.lock
